RF.put("questb:b67",{"8627":{"id":8627,"t":"Avenger's Breastplate","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nCarapace of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sage Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nAvenger's Breastplate\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"At his dwelling in Ahn'Qiraj, dread C'Thun awaits in slumber.","done":"I did not expect you to return from your attempt, ‹name›.\nYou've fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.\nBy slaying C'Thun you've not only saved all of Azeroth, you've also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.\nAccept this breastplate as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.\nMay its power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Alliance Class Paladin Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8627\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Avenger's Breastplate this quest\nBring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8707":{"id":8707,"t":"Blade of Vaulted Secrets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ornate Hilt, 2 Obsidian Idols, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ornate Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Obsidian Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlade of Vaulted Secrets\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8387":{"id":8387,"t":"Invaders of Alterac Valley","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle for Alterac rages on! You must return to Alterac Valley and once more drive the invaders out of Frostwolf territory, ‹name›!","back":"What news do you bring from the lands of the Frostwolves? How does the battle for Alterac Valley fare?","done":"Good work, ‹name›! You should be proud of yourself. The Alliance invaders must be expelled from Alterac!\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"7027":{"id":7027,"t":"Empty Stables","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate an Alterac Ram in Alterac Valley. Use the Stormpike Training Collar when you are near the Alterac Ram to 'tame' the beast. Once tamed, the Alterac Ram will follow you back to the Stable Master. Speak with the Stable Master to earn credit for the capture.\nProvided: Stormpike Training Collar","desc":"Just look at the stables, ‹name›! Empty! The Stormpike Brigade has no rams to ride - the cavalry is defunct.\nYou must help us, soldier. Take this training collar and enter the wilds of this valley. Locate the Alterac rams that roam throughout the area and use the collar to snare one. When you have captured a ram, return it to me and I shall place it in our stable.\nWhen we have enough rams, the ram rider commander will be notifed. With your help, the cavalry will be reborn!","back":"Without your help, the Stormpike Ram Riders would not have mounts to ride into battle. You do us a great service!","done":"The stables will be full in no time at all. Keep up the good work!\nStart Stormpike Stable Master Alterac Valley End Stormpike Stable Master Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7027","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"92707":{"id":92707,"t":"The giant in the den","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Goliath's Wristguards to Drum Fel in Hammerfall.\nGoliath's Wristguards","desc":"Wrenched from its hulking corpse, the goliath's bracers are massive. Your whole arm, up to the shoulder, can fit through one without touching the sides.\nYou should bring these back to Hammerfall, as a warning. Drum Fel ought to know what he's up against.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,300\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\nArathi Highlands Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Goliath's Wristguards Level 33 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 36 42 Side Horde Quest ID 92707","cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"92867":{"id":92867,"t":"Ground to keep","lv":39,"min":32,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat the Boulderfist, Syndicate, and Witherbark intruders in Stromgarde Keep and return to Groundskeeper Lomar.\nBoulderfist Mauler x 5\nSyndicate Conjuror x 3\nSyndicate Prowler x 6\nWitherbark Berserker x 3","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOld Leather Jacket Stromgarde Hood\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\nLevel 39 , requires level 32 Difficulty 32 35 37 42 49 Side Both factions Type Elite Quest ID 92867","cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6547":{"id":6547,"t":"Warsong Scout Update","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Warsong Report","rew":"You will receive:\nWarsong Scout Update","back":"Keep an eye out, ‹race›. The elves are often hiding in the shadows...\nWe must always be watching. We have worked very hard to claim this land, and the elves are looking for a chance to take it from us.\nI assume you have my next orders from Kadrak?","done":"Let Kadrak know of the success we have had here holding off the night elves. Our plans are going well.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":71,"y":68.4,"n":"Warsong Scout","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1027":{"id":1027,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":28,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the final piece of Dartol's Rod and return to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.\nIron Pommel Rusty Chest","desc":"The final piece of the rod was given to the druids of Dor'danil for safekeeping. I have no idea where they hid it. I'm sorry I can't help you more than that.\nAll I can tell you is to follow the road that leads towards the Barrens. The druids took shelter to the east of that road, but they won't be of much help to you: they were killed recently... it's something I don't like to think about much.\nWhen you find the final piece, bring it to me and I will help you reconstruct the rod.","rew":"Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Did you find the final piece of the rod, ‹name›?","done":"You found the final piece? Wonderful for you... and for Raene.\nI guess we'll have to see about repairing it, won't we?","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":53.5,"y":46.2,"n":"Shael'dryn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3907":{"id":3907,"t":"Disharmony of Fire","lv":56,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter Blackrock Depths and track down Lord Incendius. Slay him and return any source of information you may find to Thunderheart.\nTablet of Kurniya Lord Incendius\nLord Incendius slain","desc":"I can taste the foulness in the air that surrounds you, ‹name›. There is another, hidden in the depths of Blackrock, who does control this foulness.\nThe wind and earth cry his name: Lord Incendius... but someone... something... commands this being. He is merely an emissary.\nFind him and discover where his master hides. Return to me when you have collected this information.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSunborne Cape Nightfall Gloves Crypt Demon Bracers Stalwart Clutch\nMoney: 2 55 2 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,300\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The flames will soon overtake these lands. Make haste, ‹name›!","done":"<Thunderheart clutches the Tablet of Kurniya.>\nRagnaros... here...\nThe elders were right to fear the corruption emanating from Blackrock Mountain. A general of the Old Gods! IN OUR WORLD! We must reassess our position here in Kargath. We must decide on whether we stay and fight or run for fear of a new sundering.\nBe weary of any further exploration in Blackrock Mountain, ‹name›. A far greater evil than anything that exists in this world resides in those fiery depths.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3.3,"y":48.3,"n":"Thunderheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4867":{"id":4867,"t":"Urok Doomhowl","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read Warosh's Scroll. Bring Warosh's Mojo to Warosh.\nWarosh's Mojo Urok Doomhowl\nProvided: Warosh's Scroll","desc":"Argh! So hard to speak!\nTake this note! Get me my mojo!","rew":"You will receive:\nPrismcharm\nExperience: 9,950","back":"Ah! Do you have my mojo?","done":"Aha! I can already feel my powers returning to me. And my mind is no longer wracked by Urok's curse.\nThank you, ‹name›! Humility is below me, but I must acknowledge your aid.\nAnd I bid you fortune in your journeys through Blackrock Spire. You are a fool to think you could make your way to the top, but your bravery is without question.\nStart Warosh End Warosh Level 60 , requires level 55 Difficulty 55 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 4867","cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"97907":{"id":97907,"t":"Camping 101 mining","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Krunn in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your mining skill to 20","desc":"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":40.8,"n":"Krunn","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96627":{"id":96627,"t":"The adventurer","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Sam Sarsparilla near Goldshire.","desc":"‹name›, you have proven your competence as a protector thus far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Goldshire. Go and see what he's doing.","done":"I appreciate the lookin' out, ‹class›. That marshal's just a worrywart.\nHey, you've got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.8,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"8307":{"id":8307,"t":"Desert Recipe","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Look for information about cooking Sandworm Meat at the Twilight's Hammer camp west of Cenarion Hold.","desc":"Adapting to life in the desert has been difficult to say the least. Not only do I miss the birds and trees of Auberdine but our food selection is severely limited by this arid environment. I'm trying to learn about desert herbs, but there aren't many.\nI've seen Twilight's Hammer groups from the camp west of here hunt sandworms for food. Sandworm meat is so bitter though, I can't imagine how they make it palatable. Keep your eyes open if you go to their camp and let me know if you learn anything.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+10 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"This book contains several common recipes and a few unusual ones. After browsing through it for a few seconds you spot a recipe that involves sandworm meat.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.9,"y":39.2,"n":"Calandrath","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":37.9,"y":45.3,"n":"Sandy Cookbook","e":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94227":{"id":94227,"t":"Craftsmans writ big bronze knife","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Big Bronze Knife\nBig Bronze Knife","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Big Bronze Knife, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"<The chicken... clears its throat?>\nCluck, cluck.","done":"Cluck? CLUCK CLUCK! BWOK!\n<The chicken glares menacingly toward Magus Tirth from afar, newly acquired blade in beak.>","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":79.9,"y":75.7,"n":"\"Plucky\" Johnson","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94307":{"id":94307,"t":"Craftsmans writ shadoweave robe","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Shadoweave Robe\nShadoweave Robe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Shadoweave Robe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+125 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+125 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Shadoweave Robe Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94307","cats":["crafting"]},"7907":{"id":7907,"t":"Darkmoon Beast Deck","lv":55,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Beast Deck to the Darkmoon Faire when it comes to town.\nBeasts Deck","desc":"Now that you have gathered all of the Beast cards together into a deck, a ninth card mysteriously appears with the same backing as the first eight. On this card is inscribed, \"Return these cards to the Darkmoon Faire and be rewarded.\" You have heard that this faire alternately stops at Mulgore and Goldshire every few months, so you will have to wait until they are here next.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Card: Blue Dragon\nExperience: 550\n+150 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"I see that you have managed to complete a deck of Beasts! Congratulations!","done":"So you have put together a deck of Beasts. Your gesture of returning it to us will create a tie between you and the Darkmoon that will not soon be forgotten. Allow me to present you with one of the greater Darkmoon cards as a small token of our appreciation.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.4,"y":45,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.3,"y":70.1,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"947":{"id":947,"t":"Cave Mushrooms","lv":17,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Scaber Stalks and 1 Death Cap to Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine.\n5 Scaber Stalk Scaber Stalk\nDeath Cap Death Cap","desc":"I am devising a potion that requires rare mushrooms, mushrooms that grow only in a certain cave. The cave lies behind Cliffspring Falls, to the east and slightly north along the mountains.\nI would go there myself, but I was advised by the Grove of the Ancients to stay away from that place. Our venerable allies sense that the cave is the hiding place for a new evil in Darkshore.\nPlease, ‹name›, gather the mushrooms for me. And while doing so, scout the cave to confirm the Ancients' fears.","rew":"You will receive:\nGustweald Cloak 10 Red-speckled Mushroom\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Do you have my mushrooms, ‹name›? Have you been to the cave?","done":"Many thanks, ‹name›. These mushrooms are fine specimens!\nAnd when you were at Cliffspring Falls, did you find anything to confirm the warnings of the Ancients?\nThe Ancients are wise, but I had hoped that, this time, they were wrong.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.3,"y":43.6,"n":"Barithras Moonshade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98067":{"id":98067,"t":"Eyes of the sentinels","lv":11,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Place Sentinel Owls at the entrance to the Cenarion Hold depths, the Darnassus Bank, the Craftsman's Terrace Inn, and the City Gate for Sentinel Dalia Sunblade in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.\nCenarion Hold depths entrance\nDarnassus Bank\nCraftsman's Terrace Inn\nCity Gate","desc":"General Feathermoon ensures all sentinels have time to pray to Elune. A proper huntress wields not blade alone, but gifts of the goddess to overcome our enemies.\nYou may help with my daily duties. Place sentinels around the city--start with the tunnels leading beneath Cenarion Hold to the north, the bank at the center of town, the inn in the Craftsman's Terrace to the northeast, and the city gates. The guards can assist you.\nSomething is amiss in Teldrassil--we must remain vigilant.","done":"I thank you for your aid. Though I find peace in the daily rituals, it is nice to have a moment to reflect instead.\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.8,"y":89.2,"n":"Sentinel Dalia Sunblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"7507":{"id":7507,"t":"Foror's Compendium","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 7,050, 1.41 times as much.","obj":"Return Foror's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the Athenaeum.\nNostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying A Dusty Tome 0.5 % , A Dusty Tome 0.5 %\nProvided: Nostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying","desc":"You have uncovered something of great importance. This book is unlike any that you have seen.\nIt would appear as if someone or something has managed to shatter the seal of Athenaeum. The text within is garbled and barely legible.","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"Ah, one of our greatest compilations. This one has been missing for ages.","done":"You could have gotten quite a lot of gold for this book on the black market, ‹name›. Especially since the protective seal has been broken, leaving the secrets of dragon slaying viewable to any with the requisite intellect to consume the knowledge held within the sacred pages.\nPerhaps a grand reward is in order... Well, a reward that will require enormous effort to obtain.\nStart an item: Nostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7507\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 60, 26,950 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Foror's Compendium this quest\nReturn Foror's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the Athenaeum.\nNostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Forging of Quel'Serrar\nGive the Dull and Flat Elven Blade to Lorekeeper Lydros.\nA Dull and Flat Elven Blade\n7,050 XP\n3 [ 60 ] The Forging of Quel'Serrar\nYou must get Onyxia to breathe fire on the Unfired Ancient Blade.\nLorekeeper Lydros\n9,950 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"467":{"id":467,"t":"Stonegear's Search","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Pilot Stonegear.","desc":"Pilot Stonegear loves his siege engine, as every pilot should! And he's always eager to find new ways to improve his tank's firepower!\nHe heard rumors of a rare ore and is looking for someone to hunt it down for him. If your boots are starting to itch, then find Stonegear at Steelgrill's Depot in Dun Morogh and see what he wants.","rew":"Experience: 460","done":"Hello ‹name›. You're here about the task I have, eh? It's good to see a young ‹race› like yourself whose blood burns at the prospect of adventure!\nLoch Modan Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Mountaineer Kadrell","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.8,"y":36.2,"n":"Pilot Longbeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.6,"y":48.6,"n":"Pilot Stonegear","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"787":{"id":787,"t":"The New Horde","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Gornek in the Den.","desc":"Throm'ka, ‹class›. I am Eitrigg, charged by Thrall to oversee the training of recruits.\nThe Horde has changed from what it once was. There was a time where I left the Horde, disillusioned by the growing influence of the power-hungry pawns of the Burning Legion. During my exile, I was taken prisoner by a group of humans, but was rescued by the Warchief. Hearing his vision of the Horde free of demonic influence, guided by the shamans, I returned.\nGornek will have further instructions for you.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Another one of Eitrigg's recruits, hm?\nA sorry state of affairs we find ourselves in if this is the best the Horde can produce. No matter. By the time we think you're ready to leave the Valley, you'll be a proud warrior of the Horde.\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.3,"y":39.4,"n":"Eitrigg","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"67":{"id":67,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Moonbrook Schoolhouse and bring back any updated information about Stalvan to Clerk Daltry.","desc":"Stalvan, eh? Let me check the town registry.\nStalvan. . .Stalvan. . .let's see. Ah, here we go! I have a record of a Mr. Stalvan Mistmantle. The last recorded address is the Moonbrook Schoolhouse. My, talk about outdated!\nDo me a favor will you, friend? If you happen to go out to Moonbrook, let me know if you get any update on this fellow. I like to keep the records clean.","rew":"Experience: 1,150\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"The old footlocker creaks open. . . .\nDuskwood Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":41.5,"y":66.7,"n":"Old Footlocker","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"227":{"id":227,"t":"Morgan Ladimore","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Commander Althea Ebonlocke in Darkshire.","desc":"<He searches through the shelves and comes up with a leatherbound book.>\nIf you would like to know more, you might ask Althea, she's been the one to handle the... trouble... with him of late.","rew":"You will receive:\nThe Story of Morgan Ladimore\nExperience: 280\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Morgan Ladimore? Never heard of...\nOh, you mean Mor'Ladim! I guess you haven't heard the story?\nWell, I'll give you the short version. A wandering undead calling itself Mor'Ladim has been wandering Duskwood. From what we've gathered, it appears to be the undead body of Morgan Ladimore, of whom you apparently know. He's been causing us all sorts of problems, attacking Watchmen on patrol and killing people.\n<She sizes you up.>\nYou seem to be capable enough, maybe you could lay him to rest.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Sirra Von'Indi","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"8947":{"id":8947,"t":"Anthion's Strange Request","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Dark Iron Bars, 20 Enchanted Leather, 3 Mooncloth and 4 Cured Rugged Hides to Anthion Harmon in the Eastern Plaguelands.\n3 Dark Iron Bar\n20 Enchanted Leather sold by Lhara\n3 Mooncloth\n4 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"We didn't realize the importance of Valthalak's medallion, so it was divided along with the rest of the spoils. The first piece was taken by a dwarf named Theldren. I tried to retrieve it from him and he beat me within an inch of my life. You shall have to take the fragment by force.\nLast I heard of him, he'd become a gladiator for the Dark Iron dwarves. Getting him to fight you is going to present a bit of a challenge, though.\nGather the following materials for me. You're going to need them.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Did you obtain the materials I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent. I shall transmute these into something more suitable to our needs.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9187":{"id":9187,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Runic Leather Pants","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 4 Runic Leather Pants and the Craftsman's Writ - Runic Leather Pants - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Runic Leather Pants\n4 Runic Leather Pants\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Runic Leather Pants","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order LW-8485:\n4 Runic Leather Pants.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"The druids will definitely appreciate the craftsmanship that went into the making of these pants. Many thanks, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6147":{"id":6147,"t":"Return to Nathanos","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,300 experience instead of 3,400, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Return to Nathanos Blightcaller with the new information.","desc":"The Grand Crusader makes an unusual request. Hrm, regardless... what he asks will be done. Return to the Scarlet Bastion and notify him that the Oracle will be en route shortly.\nWe will take every precaution to ensure that she makes it to Stratholme unharmed.","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"The fools! My deception went unnoticed! Prepare yourself, ‹class›. We must strike with cold cunning!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":75.2,"y":71.2,"n":"Crusader Lord Valdelmar","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"147":{"id":147,"t":"Manhunt","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and kill \"the Collector\" then return to Marshal Dughan with The Collector's Ring.\nThe Collector's Ring Morgan the Collector","desc":"If the \"Collector\" is taking gold from our mines then he's stealing from the kingdom! Bring the Collector to justice, and bring me the ring mentioned in the pickup schedule you gave me. It may tell us whom the Collector is working for...\nThat Pickup Schedule says the Collector is hiding out at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. You should search for him there.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nStormwind Chain Gloves Elastic Wristguards\nExperience: 850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find the Collector? Did you discover whom he's working for?","done":"You found him? Well done, ‹name›. He won't be \"collecting\" from the Elwynn Mines again!\nAnd this ring you found is interesting... it's a membership ring for the old Stonemason's Guild in Stormwind. Why would a lowly thief have an artisan guild ring, and why are the Defias Thieves collecting money from our mines?\nDifficult questions. I hope one day we'll have answers.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4467":{"id":4467,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":44.8,"y":41.7,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8467":{"id":8467,"t":"Feathers for Nafien","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Some of the Deadwood furbolgs wear a distinctive headdress that may be used as a means of proof in thinning their numbers. Bring me a feather from any headdresses you acquire; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.\n5 Deadwood Headdress Feather Chieftain Bloodmaw 35 % , Deadwood Shaman 35 % , Deadwood Avenger 35 % , Deadwood Den Watcher 35 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"While you have proven yourself to me, you may need to continue to work toward proving yourself to the suspicious brethren of my tribe. To that end, I may be able to continue assisting you.\nSome of the Deadwood furbolgs wear a distinctive headdress that may be used as a means of proof in thinning their numbers. Bring me a feather from any headdresses you acquire; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.","done":"Well done, ‹name›! I will make sure that your deeds are known amongst my kind.\nRemember to bring any of the feathers you find to me. I will continue to accept them as long as necessary.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":64.8,"y":8.1,"n":"Nafien","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2867":{"id":2867,"t":"Return to Feathermoon Stronghold","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Shandris Feathermoon in the Feathermoon Stronghold and report your findings.","desc":"With the discovery of the strange gazebo in the heart of the Ruins of Solarsal, the time has come to return to Feathermoon Stronghold and report to General Shandris Feathermoon what has been discovered here.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,800\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Welcome back, ‹name›. Your report on this gazebo is most... disturbing. It would seem that even if the naga there were not planning on an attack, their continued presence bodes ill for our push into Feralas. At any rate, here is compensation for your investigation.\nIt would seem that Feathermoon Stronghold is in dire need of additional assistance concerning the Hatecrest naga. I'd like to offer you the task, if you are so inclined. There is much to do.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":26.3,"y":52.3,"n":"Solarsal Gazebo","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":30.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Shandris Feathermoon","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2947":{"id":2947,"t":"Return of the Ring","lv":34,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You may either keep the ring, or you may find the person responsible for the imprint and engravings on the inside of the band.\nBrilliant Gold Ring\nProvided: Brilliant Gold Ring","desc":"Opening the box produced by the Sparklematic 5200 reveals what you had suspected - a shiny ring! Wearing the ring, you feel magic power surge through you body.\nInside the band is a small but nonetheless discernable imprint of the seal of Ironforge. Next to that, three small initials are engraved: \"TdK\". This may signify either the initials of the previous owner, or perhaps the initials of the ring's crafter. Keep the ring... or return it to this person. Decisions, decisions...","rew":"Experience: 2,700","back":"Hey, easy there partner - I'm a very important businessman! I am sure that the courier is just simply late with the delivery of the rent... wait... you're not my landlord.\nWell, of course you aren't - silly me! You've come to me seeking the finest jeweler in all of Ironforge, one who does NOT make CURSED items! Yes!\nUm... what do you need?","done":"A ring, you say? Let's see... yep, I made that ring by golly.\nBefore Gnomeregan went up, I had a small shop there. Perhaps it's one I left behind when I ran for the hills; it's a simple design, and I made several like it. Maybe it's from someone who didn't make it out.\nDark Iron dwarves had this? Well, that puts a new layer of conspiracy on the nine different layers already floating about. Maybe the authorities would like to know; it's wasted on the likes of me.\nNow, back to the ring...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"547":{"id":547,"t":"Humbert's Sword","lv":30,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Ethereal Mantle.","obj":"Retrieve Deathguard Humbert's sword from Dun Garok and return it to him in Tarren Mill.\nHumbert's Sword Tamra Stormpike 8 % , Dun Garok Priest 8 % , Dun Garok Rifleman 8 % , Dun Garok Mountaineer 8 %","desc":"High Executor Darthalia sent me to keep watch of Dun Garok from a distance. I had set up camp just out of sight. But when morning came and I had to boil water, I left to gather firewood.\nWhen I returned to camp, I discovered my gear was missing.\nApparently some dwarven scouts from Dun Garok had passed by and made off with it. I need my sword! If you can get it back for me I would be so grateful. So many dwarves there...it will be quite difficult to find the dirty little thief who stole it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRibbed Breastplate Mercenary Leggings Ethereal Mantle\nNew in Forever: Ethereal Mantle.\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Were you able to retrieve my sword, ‹name›? High Executor Darthalia will hang me from the rafters if she discovers my folly.","done":"You found it!\nAh, I feel so complete with my precious sword back in my hand. Many thanks to you!","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.8,"y":20.2,"n":"Deathguard Humbert","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6067":{"id":6067,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, I do believe you are ready...\nDurotar Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"707":{"id":707,"t":"Ironband Wants You!","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Prospector Ironband at Ironband's Excavation Site in Loch Modan.","desc":"‹name›. I received reports from Prospector Ironband at his excavation site in Loch Modan--he needs some legwork done concerning another of our excavations.\nI don't have more details than that, but if you want to stretch your legs then go speak with Ironband.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"So Stormpike sent you, did he? Good.\nI have a big task for you...\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":65.9,"y":65.6,"n":"Prospector Ironband","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"6387":{"id":6387,"t":"Honor Students","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Brock's List to Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar.\nBrock's List\nProvided: Brock's List","desc":"I see a lot of young dwarves at my door, eager to learn the trade of mining. And if there's one thing a miner needs more than anything, it's a pick!\nI have a list of mining students who scored high in their lessons and earned an honorary pick. Take my list to Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge. He'll get the picks ready.\nThe fastest way to Ironforge is on a gryphon, so bring the list to our gryphon master, Thorgrum Borrelson, and speak with him about transport to Ironforge.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Ironforge\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Have you had your fill of Thelsamar so soon? Are you ready to leave for another city?","done":"You have to get this to Ironforge, eh? For a small fee I can put you on the back of one of my gryphons, and it'll take you there. How does that sound?","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37,"y":47.8,"n":"Brock Stoneseeker","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":33.9,"y":51,"n":"Thorgrum Borrelson","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"307":{"id":307,"t":"Filthy Paws","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Silver Stream Mine and collect 4 loads of Miners' Gear.\nReturn to Mountaineer Stormpike.\n4 Miners' Gear Miners' League Crates","desc":"The Silver Stream Mine to the east ran dry long ago. It was converted by the Miners' League into a storage depot, but now Kobolds have moved in, putting their filthy paws on good, Dwarven tools!\nWe'll root out those vermin soon enough, but the League wants someone to get their gear out of the mine before we warriors tromp in there and break things. It'll be a tough delve - you might want cohorts at your side.\nThe gear is stored in Miners' League Crates throughout the mine. Good luck.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIronheart Chain Robe of the Keeper Ironplate Buckler\nExperience: 1,350\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have that Miners' Gear, ‹name›?","done":"Did you see a lot of Kobolds in there? I can't wait for the order to clear them out of the mine. The thought of their grimy hands clawing around our mine makes my stomach rumble!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":24.8,"y":18.4,"n":"Mountaineer Stormpike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8867":{"id":8867,"t":"Lunar Fireworks","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Launch 8 Lunar Fireworks and 2 Cluster Fireworks and return to a Lunar Festival Harbinger at any capital city.\nLunar Fireworks Fired : 0/ 8\nLunar Fireworks Cluster Fired : 0/ 2","desc":"Every year the druids of Moonglade hold a celebration of our city's great triumph over an ancient evil.\nWe celebrate the wisdom of our elders, share in magnificent feasts and of course... shoot fireworks!\nFor a small donation you can purchase colorful rockets from our vendor. Try using some of the launchers around here, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nLunar Festival Invitation\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you find the launchers, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›.\nNow that you're in the spirit of things, why don't you take this invitation to the festival in Moonglade.\nIt's quite an enjoyable celebration, if you have the time to spare. We share food, drink, stories and of course... more fireworks!\nOpen the invitation while standing inside the circle of greater moonlight and you'll be transported to Moonglade.\nTirisfal Glades Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff Darnassus Stormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9107":{"id":9107,"t":"Plagueheart Sandals","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Sandals if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Sandals, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Sandals Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Sandals\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Sandals.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"3507":{"id":3507,"t":"Betrayed","lv":56,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.\nHead of Magus Rimtori Magus Rimtori\nProvided: Head of Magus Rimtori","desc":"Return to Belgrom in Orgrimmar. He will want to see her head for himself! We'll return there shortly.\nAh, this is indeed a good day. Thank you for your help, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPyrestone Orb Belgrom's Hammer\nExperience: 7,300\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I remember you, ‹class›. I asked you to go to Azshara to destroy that wench that betrayed me! That seems like many moons ago. Don't tell me that Ag'tor and the others are dead also!","done":"HAHA! Look at you now, pathetic woman! I spit on your remains!\nThank you, ‹name›. Thank you from the bottom of my heart! This is indeed a great day!\nI would give you a kingdom if it were in my power! But perhaps you will settle for this.\n<Belgrom looks down at the head of the mage who had betrayed him.>\nHaha! Stupid blood elf, look at you now... in a burlap sack and missing your body! You should never have betrayed Belgrom!\nAzshara Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":22.3,"y":51.5,"n":"Ag'tor Bloodfist","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Belgrom Rockmaul","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7827":{"id":7827,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.6,"y":51.2,"n":"Rashona Straglash","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"3107":{"id":3107,"t":"Consecrated Rune","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Consecrated Rune and speak to Bromos Grummner in Coldridge Valley.\nConsecrated Rune\nProvided: Consecrated Rune","desc":"While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the paladin trainer Bromos. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"So, you've made it! And not a second too soon. There's much to be done in Coldridge Valley and beyond. I'm gonna need your help as much as you're gonna need mine!\nYou're a Knight of the Silver Hand now, be ready to play the part.","done":"The humans have taught us a great deal about the Holy Light and how important their order is to them... and to protecting all of Azeroth. We have a great respect for how stepped in tradition it is, and how just one figure, one sacrifice, can make the difference between pain and salvation.\nThe two of us are gonna be working together for a bit. Any time you think you're ready, come back to me and we'll see about getting you some training. Can't have you go out into the world unprepared, now, can we?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.8,"y":68.3,"n":"Bromos Grummner","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"98387":{"id":98387,"t":"Blackrock blockade","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 10 Battleworn Axes to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.\n10 Blackrock Supplies\n8 Stolen Weapon","desc":"What the Blackrock orcs don't understand is that this is a war of attrition. Their brazen push into Alliance territory has left them vulnerable and without supplies, relying on the surrounding mountains to gather resources.\nAn army can't run on empty bellies, ‹name›. Go to their encampments south of Stonewatch Keep to the east and rob them of their food and weapons. Let's see the orcs' fighting spirit when they're starved and defenseless.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Most of what you find will have been raided from Lakeshire anyway. It will do me good to know our people will thrive while the orcs wither.","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. With the Blackrock orcs cut off from their allies in the Burning Steppes, they will have no hope of maintaining their foothold here without proper supplies.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":33.4,"y":48.8,"n":"Marshal Marris","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"78307":{"id":78307,"t":"The horn of xelthos","lv":23,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Log","desc":"Description","rew":"You will receive:\nPyrewood Signet Ring Item 203994\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,600","done":"<A note sits in the chest>\nFor ‹name›. I'll be seeing you.\n- C","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":47.1,"y":71.1,"n":"Dead Drop","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"9027":{"id":9027,"t":"Tracing the Source","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Evert Sorisam at The Finest Thread along Stormwind's Canals.","desc":"Something funny about the cologne? It's possible. I've never seen so many people after one product like this.\nLook, if there's something wrong with it, I want to know, too. I bought my supply from a merchant named Evert Sorisam. He's new in town.\nHe mentioned he had some goods he was going to deliver to The Finest Thread.","done":"Yes, of course. Those fragrances are the hottest items this season. You must be the fifth or sixth person this hour to inquire about them.\nI'm afraid my supplies are all sold out. If you'd like some, you should speak with Allison, the innkeeper of The Gilded Rose.\nYou shouldn't waste any time, though. I think you'll find the perfume will be irresistible.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.4,"y":75.3,"n":"Innkeeper Allison","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.8,"y":60.1,"n":"Evert Sorisam","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94467":{"id":94467,"t":"Call of fire","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.\nGlowing Ember\nProvided: Torch of the Dormant Flame","desc":"The fire sapta's ready, ‹name›. Now ye face the flame. Use it at the shrine, then climb to the peak. There, ye'll see the spirit--he'll not strike 'til ye do, but he'll know ye see him.\nStrike fast, lad. The longer ye wait, the stronger he burns. When he falls, take his glowing embers and place 'em in the brazier. Light the torch and earn the fire's favor.","rew":"You will receive:\nTorch of the Eternal Flame\nExperience: 1,250","back":"The brazier stands about a third your height, with charred inscriptions along its smooth metal rails. The metal shows no signs of wear from the weather, and the bowl seated at the top of it feels cool to the touch.\nBlackrock mountain looms in the distance, in clear view to honor from this sacred place.","done":"A white hot flame ignites within the bowl as you place the ember within. You can feel the magical effects of the sapta coursing through your body and the fire dances rhythmically before you.\nYou place the top of the torch within the basin, and it immediately catches on fire. The smoke seems to drift towards the mountain of blackrock.\nLoch Modan Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":32,"y":66,"n":"Braldir Ashmantle","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":31.9,"y":64.5,"n":"Brazier of the Dormant Flame","e":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":38.9,"y":58.2,"n":"Brazier of the Dormant Flame","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"7667":{"id":7667,"t":"Material Assistance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you are interested in helping Sagorne Crestrider in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom, bring him an Azerothian Diamond and a Pristine Black Diamond.\nAzerothian Diamond Hakkari Thorium Vein 1.2 % , Large Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Thorium Vein 0.7 % and 4 more\nPristine Black Diamond Veteran Commando 2.3 % , Witherbark Speaker 1 % in Zul'Gurub , Winterax Axe Thrower 1 % , Lady Illucia Barov 1 % in Scholomance and 4 more","desc":"‹name›, there is a pressing matter I hope you can help with... both materially and spiritually. Allow me to explain.\nWithin the depths of the Scholomance in Lordaeron is a chamber called the Great Ossuary. I need to complete a device that would pierce the shadows of this horrid room. To finish what I have started, I need two diamonds: an Azerothian and a Pristine Black. These are not trivial items, I know - I just don't have the resources myself.\nCould you provide me with one of each?","rew":"Experience: 4,950\n+150 reputation with Horde","back":"I feel awkward asking for material assistance, but my divination scryer - the device I hope to finish - requires one of each. If you cannot help me, I'd certainly understand.","done":"Your generosity is unrivaled, ‹name›. I thank you for your kindness.\nI will be able to finish my divination scryer now, and I should be able to fashion more without further need of diamonds... perhaps you would be interested in helping me in its use? It is for a most important task, I assure you... one that left unchecked could spell unmitigated disaster for the spirit realm!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.7,"y":35.9,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8787":{"id":8787,"t":"Armor Kits for the Field","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Rugged Armor Kits and 8 Heavy Armor Kits to Merok Longstride near Hive'Regal. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VII in order to complete this quest.\n8 Rugged Armor Kit Larion 10 % , Rabid Blisterpaw 0 % , Scorching Elemental 0 %\n8 Heavy Armor Kit Olaf 0 %\nLogistics Task Briefing VII\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing VII","desc":"The brave volunteers of the Orgrimmar Legion have arrived to Silithus to aid us in our cause. Their supplies of armor kits were somehow lost in the trip. Obtain a batch of armor kits and deliver them to Merok Longstride at the location of the Orgrimmar Legion camp.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something for me, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes... I will distribute these to the troops, ‹name›. The Orgrimmar Legion thanks you!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.9,"y":68,"n":"Merok Longstride","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"78147":{"id":78147,"t":"Crimes against anatomy","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Crimes Against Anatomy","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nCrimes Against Anatomy (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"94947":{"id":94947,"t":"Welcome to azeroth","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the Skyborne Portal to Stormwind and report to Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.\nTake the Skyborne Portal to Stormwind","desc":"Its a big world down here, and we need our people to start branching out to explore it. That's where you come in.\nThe Kirin Tor is a member of an \"Alliance\" of like-minded nations. The de-facto heart of this alliance is the city of Stormwind to the south. Elaadrin has asked me to find someone to travel to Stormwind and meet with the regent lord there, a human named Bolvar Fordragon.\nWhen you are ready, the Kirin Tor mages have set up a special portal for the High Order to use to access Stormwind.","done":"Well met, ‹class›. I am Bolvar Fordragon, regent to the throne of Stormwind.\nA Kirin Tor messenger told me to expect an emissary from the High Order, and here you stand. It's been some time since a high elf has stood in this throne room, but I am glad to accept you now as a guest.\nOn behalf of the King, I welcome you to Stormwind and give you leave to travel freely through alliance lands. Welcome to Azeroth, Skyborne.\nAlterac Mountains Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":12.4,"y":56.2,"n":"Denaaris Stargale","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78,"y":18,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"1267":{"id":1267,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":38,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Jaina Proudmore in Dustwallow Swamp.","rew":"You will receive:\nJaina's Signet Ring\nMoney: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,300\n+200 reputation with Alliance","done":"Thank you for your help ‹name›. Please accept this token of my appriciation for your efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Archmage Tervosh","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.3,"y":49,"n":"Lady Jaina Proudmoore","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"627":{"id":627,"t":"Favor for Krazek","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 loads of Lesser Bloodstone Ore to Krazek in Booty Bay.\n4 Lesser Bloodstone Ore Lesser Bloodstone Deposit","desc":"There is a mountain cave in Drywhisker Gorge, far to the north in the Arathi Highlands. In that cave is rare ore: bloodstone. The bloodstone in this cave is not of the highest grade, but even low-quality bloodstone is valuable... to those with the knowledge to use it.\nI would like some.\nI will fix your crock pot, but while I work on it... bring me samples of bloodstone. Bring me enough, and I'll even give you a bonus.\nOh, and if you don't have the skill to mine it... find someone who does!","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+75 reputation with Booty Bay\n-375 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Did you have luck getting the bloodstone?","done":"Ah, splendid! That was a big favor you did for me.\nHere is your payment...\nStranglethorn Vale Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8227":{"id":8227,"t":"Nat's Measuring Tape","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 950, 0.68 times as much.","obj":"Return Nat's Measuring Tape to Nat Pagle in Dustwallow Marsh.\nNat's Measuring Tape\nProvided: Nat's Measuring Tape","desc":"Amongst the shattered fishing lures and tackle is a rolled, silken measuring tape. Attached to the tape is a label that reads:\n\"Nat Pagle, Dustwallow Marsh.\"","rew":"Experience: 650","back":"Hello there, laddie/lassy. You here to do some fishing?","done":"Why, you found my favorite measuring tape! I love this tape! I measured some of the biggest fish I ever caught with it...\nBut, I lost this tape in Zul'Gurub... you've been to Zul'Gurub? Did you see the fabled Gahz'ranka?\nWell... do you want to catch him?","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":58.6,"y":60.1,"n":"Nat Pagle","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8067":{"id":8067,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Predator's Mantle","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring the following Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub to Falthir the Sightless: A Primal Hakkari Aegis. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Aegis\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"We Zandalar prize what we wear as a symbol of accomplishment. You don't need to be able to see what one wears to be able to sense what emanates from it - power transcends sight. The garments of the Zandalar predator are like this, and most cherished by them is the mantle they wear. It helps to obfuscate them from view... and to make their presence known when they wish it.\nThe Paragons of Power await your retrieval in Zul'Gurub. Bring me what I seek, and the predator's mantle shall be yours.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Predator's Mantle\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Have your strikes into Zul'Gurub yielded success, ‹name›? Only when you've brought me what I seek - and proven yourself fully to the tribe - will you earn a mantle second to none amongst the Zandalar.","done":"Success... you are to be revered amongst the tribe, ‹name›. It was no small feat acquiring the Paragons of Power needed for the mantle, but you handled it in the fashion of the deadliest of our predators. You've earned your place amongst them, and you've certainly earned the right to wear their mantle.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1427":{"id":1427,"t":"Threat From the Sea","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tok'Kar in the Swamp of Sorrows.","desc":"Before you take rest, speak to Tok'Kar again. While you were gone I believe he finished a few weapons. For your help here, he would offer one of them to you. You would do well to test its strength against the fish men when you are ready... but only to please me further.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTok'kar's Murloc Shanker Tok'kar's Murloc Basher Tok'kar's Murloc Chopper\nExperience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Ah, ‹name›, you've returned. Good. I've finished crafting more weapons for our fight against the murlocs. For bringing us the fresh sawtooth meat, and for bringing a small smile to Katar's face, I offer one of them to you.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":83.8,"y":80.4,"n":"Katar","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":81.3,"y":81,"n":"Tok'Kar","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"867":{"id":867,"t":"Harpy Raiders","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 8 Witchwing talons.\nReturn them to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.\n8 Witchwing Talon Serena Bloodfeather 39 % , Witchwing Windcaller 39 % , Witchwing Ambusher 39 % , Witchwing Slayer 39 % and 2 more","desc":"The blasted harpies have been ravaging our caravan supplies for too long. It's time we slit a few of their throats and diminished their numbers.\nI've been snooping around their nests and figured out who leads who. The most devastating attack will destroy a good section of their lower chain of command and then we can work our way to the top.\nI'll start you off slow, take out Witchwing Harpies and Witchwing Roguefeathers in the Northwest and bring me 8 Witchwing talons. That should be a good start...","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Cut up enough of them yet? Keep slicing and taking trophies. I want 8 Witchwing talons.","done":"Oh, these are nice. Real nice... Good job, ‹name›. I look forward to seeing more of your work in the future.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.6,"y":30.9,"n":"Darsok Swiftdagger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"95507":{"id":95507,"t":"Vrangs game","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Trapped Game from traps found in Sprung Traps in the Barrens.\n8 Trapped Game","desc":"While you are out there, it would be of great help to me if you could check on my traps for me. I've got them strewn all over the valley.\nBring back any small game that I've caught. Keep your eye out for the other wildlife, though. This area can be dangerous if you aren't paying attention.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"<Vrang grunts at you as you approach.>","done":"Thank you for your aid, ‹class›. I was starting to wonder if I'd have to go to bed hungry tonight because this cursed wound on my leg.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.8,"y":12.2,"n":"Vrang Wildgore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"9267":{"id":9267,"t":"Mending Old Wounds","lv":60,"min":15,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"40 Linen Cloth Kogan Forgestone , Lisan Pierce , Adam Lind 66.7 % , Hidden Strongbox 58.6 % and 4 more\n4 Empty Vial sold by Tharynn Bouden , sold by Amy Davenport , sold by Gina MacGregor , sold by Antonio Perelli and 4 more","back":"You'd better think twice before setting foot in Ratchet, ‹name›! Word's been getting around of your dirty deeds.\nYou're in luck though, a ship just arrived with many wounded from an encounter with the Bloodsail Buccaneers. This is your chance to prove you're not a complete scoundrel. Lend us a hand by bringing linen cloth for bandages and empty vials for potions.","done":"I'm happy you're seeing the error of your ways, ‹name›. Keep the supplies coming; we're not going to forget about you so easily, mister/miss!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":61.2,"y":37.9,"n":"Mupsi Shacklefridd","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4787":{"id":4787,"t":"The Ancient Egg","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Ancient Egg to Yeh'kinya in Tanaris.\nAncient Egg Ancient Egg","desc":"The Prophecy of Mosh'aru speaks of an ancient egg. It is a relic of a time when trolls ruled vast empires, and it has the power to hold the essence of Hakkar. It may be the only way to keep our world safe from his evil.\nBring me the ancient egg, ‹name›. It is said to lay hidden deep within Jintha'Alor in the Hinterlands, in a cave behind the amphitheater at the top of the city.","rew":"Experience: 5,900","back":"Do you have the ancient egg? I sense great forces stirring, and I fear that time grows short.","done":"Ah, you have the egg! I bow to you, ‹name›. Your strength and bravery will be long remembered.\nTanaris Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67,"y":22.4,"n":"Yeh'kinya","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"387":{"id":387,"t":"Quell The Uprising","lv":26,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Quell The Uprising. Pays 40s instead of 60s. Gives 5,550 experience instead of 2,650, 2.09 times as much. Partly read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved wh","obj":"Warden Thelwater of Stormwind wants you to kill 10 Defias Prisoners, 8 Defias Convicts, and 8 Defias Insurgents in The Stockade.\nDefias Prisoner slain : 0/ 10\nDefias Convict slain : 0/ 8\nDefias Insurgent slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The uprising must be quelled! I need your assistance. If word gets out that the prison is overrun I will lose my job! This is a case of foul play if I've ever seen one. But what's important now is forcing these prisoners into submission for the safety of Stormwind.\nThe punishment for insurgency is death. Kill some of these deviants! That ought to get things under control.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The Stockade is still overrun! These Defias Rats must be shown that their actions will not be tolerated. Now get back down there and show some force!","done":"Your efforts in The Stockade were valiant, ‹name›. It's obvious this problem is bigger than the both of us. But you have performed well and for that I am thankful.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.5,"y":69.4,"n":"Warden Thelwater","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-stockade"]},"6627":{"id":6627,"t":"Test of Lore","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Answer Braug Dimspirit's question successfully and then speak to him again. He will remain in Stonetalon Mountains when you are ready.","desc":"You have brought me the book, and now it is time for your question. Are you ready?\nTime is not an issue, ‹class›, so do not feel pressured. You may take as long as you like to answer.","rew":"Experience: 250","back":"Life is full of questions, ‹class›. You will never be able to answer all of them, but with some time and study, perhaps you will become a little more knowledgeable.","done":"Well done, ‹class›. You have studied the text I asked you to, and now you have passed another of our tests.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":78.8,"y":45.7,"n":"Braug Dimspirit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1107":{"id":1107,"t":"Encrusted Tail Fins","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 75s instead of 35s.","obj":"Bring 10 Encrusted Tail Fins to Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\n10 Encrusted Tail Fin Saltscale Hunter 80 % , Saltscale Forager 80 % , Saltscale Tide Lord 80 % , Saltscale Oracle 80 % and 1 more","desc":"Our rocket car is the fastest thing on the flats! So fast that ... I'm afraid friction is going to tear it apart!\nTo prevent that I need to create a composite to coat the car's moving parts. It must be hard but not brittle, and must be resistant to salt corrosion, or time spent on the Shimmering Flats will eat it away.\nHave you heard of the Vile Reef, ‹name›? It's off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale. Saltscale murlocs live there, and their tail fins are a crucial ingredient of my composite.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450","back":"Do you have the tail fins? If I can't protect our car from its own speed, then it won't last long in these races.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›! After I grind these down and fuse them with a few other ingredients, the composite will be ready. And after that, the car will be safe from its own speed.\nSafe, as long as it doesn't hit anything...\nThousand Needles Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Wizzle Brassbolts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1187":{"id":1187,"t":"Razzeric's Tweaking","lv":41,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Seaforium Booster for Razzeric in the Shimmering Flats.\nSeaforium Booster Gizmorium Shipping Crate","desc":"Pozzik's a great mechanic, I know that, but he's afraid to just load on the firepower and grab on for the ride. Not me, though.\nAfter Pozzik finishes with a racer, I take a little time to put my own modifications on--you know, loosening up the controls, removing parts of the frame, and adding more juice!\nI ordered a seaforium booster from Shreev at the Gizmorium in Gadgetzan, but apparently the zeppelin it was being sent on crashed in Dustwallow Marsh! I gotta have it, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,300\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"How'm I supposed to show my face around the track without a little extra kick to get me going? It's a travesty, I tell you.","done":"Just take a look at this beauty! Fifteen pounds of solid seaforium power! Once I get this strapped on to the side of my racer, I'll be around the track so fast I'll beat the gnomes twice!\nThousand Needles Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.3,"y":76.1,"n":"Razzeric","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"4147":{"id":4147,"t":"Marvon's Workshop","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Marvon Rivetseeker's workshop in Ratchet.","desc":"I managed to spy on what Muigin was doing, and he's actually growing the darn things over there!\nI think the only solution here is to... no, not go talk to him... What are you thinking? The solution is to fight back!\nWe'll need the help of my friend, Marvon, who has a workshop in Ratchet. I'm sure he'll be able to create some sort of gadget that will help us.","rew":"Experience: 2,550","done":"Marvon's been gone quite a long time now, ‹name›. He went off to Tanaris to study some of the ancient troll ruins.\nNow, what was it that you said you needed?\nUn'Goro Crater The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":45.5,"y":8.7,"n":"Larion","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":38.7,"n":"Liv Rizzlefix","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1507":{"id":1507,"t":"Devourer of Souls","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Cazul in the Cleft of Shadow.","desc":"The time has come for you to learn more of the summoning magics. You will learn to summon a succubus, a creature of incredible mental powers. It can lull those of weak minds into its servitude--but have no fear! I feel certain that you will be equal to the challenge.\nA succubus can only be summoned when baited with an item that represents great devotion and love. I leave it to you to find such an object.\nA suggestion? Speak with Cazul... There seems to be little the ancient warlock does not know.","rew":"Experience: 160","done":"Hm... ‹name›. You are still new to your path, but I sense the possibility for greatness in you.\nYou were born with gifts, ‹name›. See that they do not go to waste.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.3,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":47.1,"y":46.4,"n":"Cazul","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1667":{"id":1667,"t":"Dead-tooth Jack","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Haggard's Badge from Dead-tooth Jack's camp, and return to Marshal Haggard.\nMarshal Haggard's Badge Dead-tooth's Strongbox","desc":"Burlguard sent you, did he? Yes, I have spare weapons around here, but first I have a task for you...\nA while ago a Defias villain Dead-tooth Jack tricked me. It was dark and he was wearing a Stormwind tabard and I thought he was Marshal Dughan. He said he needed my old Stormwind Marshal's badge and I gave it to him... and then he laughed and ran off before I could catch him!\nGet back my badge! Dead-tooth Jack probably has it stowed in his camp to the south.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHaggard's Axe Haggard's Hammer Haggard's Dagger Haggard's Sword\nExperience: 850","back":"Do you have my badge? I don't want to think of the mischief Dead-tooth Jack could cause with it.","done":"Great, you found it! I feared it was gone forever, used by the Defias to impersonate a Stormwind official. Well that won't happen now, thanks to you.\nHere are some weapons I used when I was a Marshal. I kept them in great shape--take your pick!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.6,"y":69.4,"n":"Marshal Haggard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5507":{"id":5507,"t":"Mantles of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Lightspark at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\n10 Argent Dawn Valor Token\nReach 21000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Your service to the Argent Dawn is to be commended, ‹name›. You are truly revered amongst us. I have been authorized to make available for you to purchase one of the Dawn's most valued items - our magic resistance mantles.\nApplication of a mantle to your existing shoulder piece will enhance your resistance to the powers of magic in one of five potential ways. As a sign of continued dedication to our cause, I ask for no less than ten of our valor tokens in exchange for access to these mantles.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Ah, noble ‹class›! Have you brought the valor tokens requested of you? Once you hand them to me, I will make our various mantles available to you for purchase.","done":"Outstanding - your tribute to the Dawn is duly noted, ‹name›. With this accomplished, I am delighted to make our mantles available to you for purchase. So long as you maintain your current status with us, these mantles will be purchasable from any authorized quartermaster of the Argent Dawn.\nFor the Dawn, my brother/sister!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.8,"y":83.7,"n":"Argent Quartermaster Lightspark","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92467":{"id":92467,"t":"Call of earth","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Rise of Spirits and drink the Earth Sapta.\nEarth Sapta","desc":"A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.\nThe sapta is always drunk in a sacred place, and never anywhere else--remember that.\nSeek out the Rise of Spirits up the pass northeast of here. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you will see what you need see.","done":"Ah... ‹name›... child of the four winds... You seek understanding. You seek answers. Why have the winds left you? How may you get them back? These are answers I cannot provide, for I do not know the motives or movements of the winds.\nI can, however, teach you much of the earth. Its strength, its resolve. Even here, high in this endless sea of clouds, you are still a creature of the earth. If you hope to find the strength to speak to the spirits of the four winds once more, this is the path you must walk.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.7,"y":23.5,"n":"Windshaper Boro","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":49.6,"y":24,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92947":{"id":92947,"t":"Making our move","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 7 Al'Aketh Guardians, 7 Al'Aketh Spiritcallers, and 7 Al'Aketh Blademasters, then report to Hyusaa Quickbreeze at the Shrine of Akir.\nAl'Aketh Guardian slain : 0/ 7\nAl'Aketh Spiritcaller slain : 0/ 7\nAl'Aketh Blademaster slain : 0/ 7\nReport to Hyusaa Quickbreeze","desc":"Everyone is here, good. I've just sent a few of my best fighters in through the front of the shrine to cause a bit of trouble and serve as a distraction, while I lead the Windshapers and High Order in from the flank.\nIf all goes well, we should be able to punch through quickly and take out the High Priestess. As for you, get in there and start cracking skulls. Meet my second, Hyusaa Quickbreeze, near the steps to the shrine after you've caused some trouble.\nWinds guide you, ‹class›.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"We fought hard to get this far but it isn't over yet.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.2,"y":71,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":63.8,"y":50.4,"n":"Hyusaa Quickbreeze","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8147":{"id":8147,"t":"The Maelstrom's Tendril","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Maelstrom's Tendril","rew":"You will receive:\nMaelstrom's Tendril\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Ah, ‹name›, it is good to smell you again.\n<Falthir grins.>\nYou'll have to excuse my sense of humor. It can be most foul at times.\nI sense that you have caused great anguish to our enemies. The forces of Hakkar cry out your name in anger. This is most excellent.\nYou have earned another weave on your talisman. Hand it to me.","done":"Let them seek atonement at the end of your munitions.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});